        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4376,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1902,
        "paragraph_id": "42C56AFC",
        "text": "Time integration scheme"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 89754,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4377,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1903,
        "paragraph_id": "2AA6296E",
        "text": "The time integration of the mass and momentum balance equations is combined in an explicit leap-frog scheme, as depicted in Figure C.3. The velocities (in the '-' points) are updated using the momentum balance. The water levels are updated using the mass balance. The water level gradients influence the momentum balance and the velocities and derived discharges affect the mass balance. Because of the leap-frog scheme these influences are always computed at the half time step level, which makes the scheme second order accurate."
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
